  "details": "Im not entirely sure if this is user error but when creating an avatar in unity 2022 / 2019 and setting the viewpoint, when getting in play mode and letting the animator do its thing, the avatar suddenly shifts a bit.\n\nI noticed this behaviour on lots of avatars I bought from various different creators or made on my own.\n\nIts often only a very slight shift which isnt really noticeable, so i can imagine most dont see it or its just to few of a change to be causing issues.\n\nOn one avatar this change was really noticeable though and caused the viewpoint to be all the way inside the head instead of just between the eyes.\n\nI think it could be related to the stand still default animation moving the root bone in some way? So either its an issue with the sdk or I would love to know how to prevent shifts like this in the first place.\n\nAttached are some pictures of some avatars with before play mode and after (with gesture manager) and one where I put them over each other to better show the difference. Specially on the red haired one its verx noticeable how much the avatar position in relation to the viewball changes. Also I made sure to have a completly fresh Avatar Descriptor on the red haired avatar. So no custom FX or anything.",
